@startuml system-boundary
title System Boundary ; per ADR-ES-027 + CR-ES-027

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

class "Entity" as Ent
class "System" as Sys
class "Element" as Elem
class "Boundary" as Bnd
class "Context" as Ctx
class "Function" as Fn
class "Purpose" as Purp
class "Outcome" as Out
class "Behavior" as Bhv
class "Capability" as Cap
class "Service" as Svc
class "Workflow" as Wf
class "Agent" as Ag

Ent <|-- Sys : specializes

Sys --> Elem : contains
Sys --> Bnd : has
Sys --> Ctx : operates-within
Sys --> Fn : realizes
Sys --> Purp : realizes
Sys --> Out : produces
Sys --> Bhv : exhibits
Sys --> Cap : supports
Sys --> Svc : implements
Sys --> Wf : participates-in
Sys --> Ag : engages

note right of Sys
  Per ADR-ES-027 section 6 + Recon-ES-004:
  System is NOT Entity (too broad)
  System is NOT Organization (requires people + roles)
  System is NOT Service (delivery-oriented)
  System is NOT Resource (consumable)
  System is NOT Process (activity sequence)
  System is NOT Workflow (execution-oriented)
  System is NOT Capability (functional ability)
  System is NOT IT system specifically
end note

@enduml
